      "output": {
        "message": "To stay close without putting on an act, a couple of approaches can help: 1. **Keep your words brief and completely true.** You don't have to perform high-energy hype. A calm, direct statement like, \"I'm genuinely really happy for you\" expresses the real support you feel without requiring you to fake enthusiasm you don't have.\n2. **Anchor your time together on other things.** You don't have to make the scholarship the main topic of conversation. Once you've acknowledged the win, steer your hangouts back toward the shared interests, humor, or everyday stuff that your friendship is normally built on. If you are close enough that openness feels safe, you can even be lightly honest: \"I'm really glad for you, even though part of me is feeling a bit envious right now.\" But if that feels like too much, sticking to simple, authentic support and regular topics works well.",
